          "funFact": "Did you know? An {name} has three hearts and blue blood! It is very smart and can open jars. Octopuses change color and texture to camouflage.",
          "try": "Spell {name} and wiggle eight fingers like arms!"
        },
        "crab": {
          "about": "{name} is a sea animal with a hard shell and two strong claws. It walks sideways on the beach or ocean floor. {name} hides under rocks and pinches if you bother it.",
          "funFact": "Did you know? {name}s grow new shells as they get bigger! They breathe with gills. Crabs can run quickly sideways to escape.",
          "try": "Spell {name} and scuttle sideways like a crab!"
        },
        "lobster": {
          "about": "{name} is a large sea creature with a long body and big claws. It lives on the rocky ocean floor and hides in crevices. {name} has a hard shell and long antennae to feel around.",
          "funFact": "Did you know? Some {name}s can live over 100 years! They walk on the sea bottom at night to hunt. Lobsters can regrow a lost claw over time.",
          "try": "Spell {name} and snap your hands like big claws!"
        },
        "pufferfish": {
          "about": "{name} is a round fish that can puff up like a balloon when afraid. It has spines that stick out when inflated. {name} swims slowly in warm seas and coral reefs.",
          "funFact": "Did you know? Some {name}s are poisonous if eaten! They fill with water or air to look too big to swallow. Pufferfish have beak-like teeth.",
          "try": "Spell {name} and puff your cheeks out big!"
        },
        "seal": {
          "about": "{name} is a furry sea animal with flippers that swims and rests on beaches or ice. It has whiskers to feel fish in dark water. {name} barks or growls and loves to play in waves.",
          "funFact": "Did you know? A {name} can hold its breath a long time underwater! Seal pups have fluffy white fur. Seals are great at catching fish.",
          "try": "Spell {name} and clap your hands like flippers!"
        },
        "tropicalFish": {
          "about": "{name} is a bright colorful fish that lives near warm coral reefs. It has beautiful patterns that help it hide among plants. {name} swims in sunny shallow water with many other fish.",
          "funFact": "Did you know? Reef {name} often clean bigger fish by eating parasites! Their colors warn predators or attract mates. Many need clean warm oceans to survive.",
          "try": "Spell {name} and swim with wiggly rainbow fingers!"
        },
        "seashell": {
          "about": "{name} is the hard home that a soft sea animal once lived inside. Waves wash shells onto sandy beaches for you to find. {name} can be spiral, smooth, or bumpy in many colors.",
          "funFact": "Did you know? You can hear the ocean sound when you hold a {name} to your ear — that is really the air moving inside! Shells are made of calcium like chalk. Hermit crabs borrow empty shells.",
          "try": "Spell {name} and cup your ear like listening to the sea!"
        },
        "seaTurtle": {
          "about": "{name} is a reptile with a hard shell that lives in the ocean. It has flippers to swim long distances and comes to sandy beaches to lay eggs. {name} can live many decades if kept safe.",
          "funFact": "Did you know? A {name} returns to the beach where it was born to nest! They breathe air but can stay underwater a long time. Plastic bags in the ocean can hurt turtles.",
          "try": "Spell {name} and paddle your arms like slow flippers!"
        },
        "shrimp": {
          "about": "{name} is a small sea animal with a curved body and long antennae. It swims backward quickly by flipping its tail. {name} is food for fish, whales, and people in many places.",
          "funFact": "Did you know? Some {name} can make a loud snapping sound with one claw! Shrimp come in many colors, even see-through. They clean parasites off fish on reefs.",
          "try": "Spell {name} and flick your finger like a flipping tail!"
        },
        "squid": {
          "about": "{name} is a fast sea animal with ten arms, including two longer tentacles. It shoots ink and jets through the water to escape hunters. {name} has big eyes and a soft body shaped like a torpedo.",
          "funFact": "Did you know? Giant {name} can grow as long as a school bus! Squid change color with special cells in their skin. They are related to octopuses.",
          "try": "Spell {name} and shoot backward with your arms behind you!"
        }
      }
