  "stories": {
    "title": "Stories",
    "header": "Story Time",
    "description": "Beautiful stories with morals — festivals, family, and more!",
    "pickStory": "wonderful stories to read!",
    "prevStory": "Previous Story",
    "nextStory": "Next Story",
    "readNow": "Read now",
    "minRead": "min",
    "readAloud": "Read story aloud",
    "tapToPause": "Story playing — tap to pause",
    "listenAgain": "Listen again",
    "moralTitle": "Moral of the Story",
    "progress": "Story {current} of {total}",
    "items": {
      "diwali": {
        "title": "The Story of Diwali",
        "subtitle": "The Festival of Lights",
        "moral": "Good always triumphs over evil, and truth and kindness bring light into our lives.",
        "p1": "Long ago, there was a kind and brave prince named Rama, who lived in the beautiful kingdom of Ayodhya. He always followed the path of truth, respected everyone, and helped people in need. One day, Rama, his wife Sita, and his loyal brother Lakshmana went to live in the forest for fourteen years to honor his father's promise.",
        "p2": "While they were living in the forest, the demon king Ravana kidnapped Sita and took her to the island kingdom of Lanka. Rama set out to rescue her with the help of Hanuman, the brave Vanara army, and many loyal friends. After a great battle, Rama defeated Ravana, rescued Sita, and restored peace.",
        "p3": "When the fourteen years ended, Rama, Sita, and Lakshmana returned to Ayodhya. The people of Ayodhya were overjoyed to welcome them home. They cleaned their houses, decorated the streets, and lit thousands of diyas (oil lamps) to celebrate their return. The bright lights filled the entire city with happiness and hope.",
        "p4": "Since then, people celebrate Diwali, the Festival of Lights. Families decorate their homes with diyas and rangoli, wear new clothes, share sweets, pray together, and spend time with their loved ones. Diwali reminds us that goodness, truth, and kindness always triumph over evil."
      },
      "holi": {
        "title": "The Story of Holi",
        "subtitle": "The Festival of Colors",
        "moral": "Truth, faith, and kindness are always stronger than evil.",
        "p1": "Long ago, there lived a kind and devoted boy named Prahlad. He was a great devotee of Lord Vishnu and always chose the path of truth, kindness, and goodness. However, his father, King Hiranyakashipu, wanted everyone to worship only him and became angry because Prahlad continued to worship Lord Vishnu.",
        "p2": "The king tried many ways to stop Prahlad, but Prahlad's faith never changed. Finally, Hiranyakashipu asked his sister Holika to sit in a fire with Prahlad. Holika had received a special boon that protected her from fire. She believed this boon would keep her safe while Prahlad would be harmed.",
        "p3": "According to the traditional story, because Holika misused her boon for a wrong purpose, the boon did not protect her. Holika was burned in the fire, but Prahlad remained safe through the blessings of Lord Vishnu and his unwavering faith.",
        "p4": "People remember this victory of good over evil by celebrating Holika Dahan on the evening before Holi. The next day, families and friends celebrate Holi, the Festival of Colors. They play with bright colors, sing, dance, share sweets, and wish happiness to everyone.",
        "p5": "Holi teaches us to let go of anger, forgive others, spread kindness, and celebrate love, friendship, and togetherness."
      },
      "ganesh_chaturthi": {
        "title": "The Story of Ganesh Chaturthi",
        "subtitle": "The God of Wisdom and New Beginnings",
        "moral": "Obey your parents, respect others, and always choose wisdom and kindness.",
        "p1": "Long ago, Goddess Parvati wished to have someone who would always protect her. According to the traditional story, she made a young boy from sandalwood paste and gave him life. She named him Ganesha and asked him to guard the entrance while she was inside.",
        "p2": "After some time, Lord Shiva returned home and wanted to enter. Ganesha did not know who Lord Shiva was and politely stopped him because he was following his mother's instructions. A misunderstanding took place, and in anger, Lord Shiva cut off Ganesha's head.",
        "p3": "When Goddess Parvati learned what had happened, she became very sad. To make things right, Lord Shiva promised to bring Ganesha back to life. He asked his followers to bring the head of the first living being they found facing north, which was an elephant. Lord Shiva placed the elephant's head on Ganesha's body and brought him back to life.",
        "p4": "Lord Shiva blessed Ganesha and declared that he would be worshipped before the beginning of every important work. Since then, Lord Ganesha has been known as the God of Wisdom, Knowledge, and New Beginnings.",
        "p5": "Every year, people celebrate Ganesh Chaturthi with great joy. Families welcome Lord Ganesha's idol into their homes, decorate with flowers, sing prayers, offer sweets like modak, and pray for wisdom, happiness, and success. After the celebration, the idol is respectfully immersed in water, reminding everyone that life is a beautiful cycle of new beginnings."
      },
      "christmas": {
        "title": "The Story of Christmas",
        "subtitle": "A Celebration of Love and Peace",
        "moral": "Love everyone, help others, and always share kindness and happiness.",
        "p1": "Long ago, in the town of Bethlehem, a baby named Jesus was born to Mary and Joseph. According to the Christian tradition, Jesus was born in a simple stable because there was no room available at the inn. Baby Jesus was gently placed in a manger filled with soft hay.",
        "p2": "On the night Jesus was born, a bright star shone in the sky. Angels shared the joyful news with nearby shepherds, who happily came to visit the baby. Later, three wise men followed the bright star to Bethlehem. They brought special gifts of gold, frankincense, and myrrh to honor Jesus.",
        "p3": "As Jesus grew up, he taught people to love one another, help those in need, forgive others, and live with kindness, peace, and compassion. His teachings continue to inspire millions of people around the world.",
        "p4": "Today, people celebrate Christmas on 25th December. Families decorate Christmas trees, sing joyful carols, exchange gifts, share delicious meals, and spend happy time together. Many people also help those in need, remembering the message of love and generosity that Christmas represents.",
        "p5": "Christmas reminds us to fill our hearts with love, kindness, peace, and the joy of giving."
      },
      "eid_ul_fitr": {
        "title": "The Story of Eid-ul-Fitr",
        "subtitle": "A Festival of Gratitude and Togetherness",
        "moral": "Be thankful, help those in need, and spread kindness and joy with everyone.",
        "p1": "Eid-ul-Fitr is a joyful festival celebrated by Muslims around the world. It marks the end of the holy month of Ramadan, a special month during which many Muslims fast from dawn until sunset. During Ramadan, people spend more time praying, reading the Holy Quran, helping those in need, and practicing kindness, patience, and gratitude.",
        "p2": "When the new moon is seen, Ramadan ends and Eid-ul-Fitr begins. On the morning of Eid, families wear clean or new clothes and gather for a special prayer called the Eid prayer. Before the prayer, Muslims give Zakat al-Fitr, a special charity that helps people in need so everyone can celebrate the festival with happiness.",
        "p3": "After the prayer, families and friends greet each other by saying \"Eid Mubarak,\" which means \"Blessed Eid.\" They visit relatives and friends, enjoy delicious meals, share sweets, exchange gifts, and spend joyful time together. Children are often given small gifts or money called Eidi, making the festival even more exciting for them.",
        "p4": "Eid-ul-Fitr is a celebration of gratitude, generosity, forgiveness, and togetherness. It reminds everyone to care for others, share with those in need, and spread love and happiness in the community."
      },
      "raksha_bandhan": {
        "title": "The Story of Raksha Bandhan",
        "subtitle": "The Bond of Love and Protection",
        "moral": "Love, respect, and caring make family bonds strong and beautiful.",
        "p1": "Raksha Bandhan is a beautiful Indian festival that celebrates the special bond of love, care, and protection between brothers and sisters. The name Raksha Bandhan means \"the bond of protection.\"",
        "p2": "On this special day, sisters tie a colorful thread called a Rakhi around their brothers' wrists. The Rakhi is a symbol of love, trust, and good wishes. Brothers promise to care for, respect, and support their sisters, and sisters pray for their brothers' happiness, good health, and success.",
        "p3": "Families celebrate the festival by wearing traditional clothes, performing a small prayer, applying tilak, tying the Rakhi, exchanging sweets, and giving thoughtful gifts. Today, Raksha Bandhan is also celebrated between cousins, friends, and even people who wish to express love, respect, and care for one another.",
        "p4": "Raksha Bandhan teaches us that true strength comes from love, respect, trust, and caring for our family and loved ones. It reminds us to protect not only our brothers and sisters but also to be kind, responsible, and supportive toward everyone."
      },
      "lion_and_mouse": {
        "title": "The Lion and the Mouse",
        "subtitle": "A tiny friend can save the day",
        "moral": "Never judge anyone by their size. Even the smallest friend can make a big difference.",
        "p1": "One sunny afternoon, a mighty lion was sleeping peacefully under a large tree in the forest. A tiny little mouse was playing nearby with its friends. While running around, the mouse accidentally climbed onto the lion's back. The lion suddenly woke up and caught the little mouse with his big paw.",
        "p2": "\"Please let me go. I am very sorry. One day, I may be able to help you,\" said the frightened mouse. The lion laughed because he could not imagine how such a small mouse could ever help a strong lion. Still, the lion was kind and decided to let the little mouse go free.",
        "p3": "A few days later, the lion was walking through the forest when he became trapped in a hunter's strong net. He roared loudly for help, but no matter how hard he tried, he could not escape.",
        "p4": "The little mouse heard the lion's roar and quickly ran to help. Without wasting any time, the mouse began to nibble the ropes of the net with its sharp little teeth. Slowly, the ropes became weaker until they finally broke. The lion was free again.",
        "p5": "The lion smiled and thanked the little mouse. He realized that even someone small can do great things. From that day on, the lion and the mouse became good friends and always helped each other whenever they could."
      },
      "hare_and_tortoise": {
        "title": "The Hare and the Tortoise",
        "subtitle": "Slow and steady wins the race",
        "moral": "Slow and steady wins the race. Patience, hard work, and determination lead to success.",
        "p1": "One day, a fast hare loved to boast about how quickly he could run. He often laughed at a slow-moving tortoise and said, \"No one can beat me in a race!\"",
        "p2": "The tortoise smiled and calmly replied, \"Let's have a race and find out.\" The forest animals gathered to watch the exciting race. When the race began, the hare ran very fast and soon disappeared far ahead of the tortoise.",
        "p3": "After running a long distance, the hare looked back and saw that the tortoise was still far behind. Feeling very confident, the hare thought, \"I have plenty of time. I'll take a short nap.\" He lay down under a shady tree and quickly fell asleep.",
        "p4": "Meanwhile, the tortoise kept walking slowly without stopping. Step by step, he moved closer to the finish line. He never gave up, even though he was much slower than the hare.",
        "p5": "After some time, the hare woke up and rushed toward the finish line as fast as he could. But it was too late. The tortoise had already crossed the finish line and won the race. All the animals cheered happily for the tortoise. The hare learned that being talented is not enough if we become careless. Success comes to those who stay focused, work hard, and never give up."
      },
      "ant_and_grasshopper": {
        "title": "The Ant and the Grasshopper",
        "subtitle": "Prepare today for a better tomorrow",
        "moral": "Hard work, preparation, and planning today help us face tomorrow with confidence.",
        "p1": "On a warm summer day, a group of hardworking ants was busy collecting tiny grains of food. They carried the food back to their home one by one. Even though the work was difficult, the ants knew they had to prepare for the cold winter, when food would be hard to find.",
        "p2": "Nearby, a cheerful grasshopper was singing, dancing, and enjoying the sunny weather. He watched the ants working and laughed. \"Why are you working so hard?\" he asked. \"Come and play with me instead!\"",
        "p3": "One of the ants smiled and replied, \"We are collecting food for the winter. It is important to be prepared for the future.\" But the grasshopper did not listen. He continued to play every day without thinking about what would happen when the seasons changed.",
        "p4": "Soon, winter arrived. The weather became cold, and the ground was covered with snow. There were no green plants or fresh food to eat. The grasshopper became hungry and realized that he had nothing stored for the winter.",
        "p5": "The ants had plenty of food because they had worked hard during the summer. Seeing the grasshopper in need, they reminded him that planning ahead is important. The grasshopper understood his mistake and promised that from then on, he would work hard and prepare for the future. From that day, he learned the value of hard work, responsibility, and good planning."
      },
      "please_and_thank_you": {
        "title": "The Power of Saying \"Please\" and \"Thank You\"",
        "subtitle": "Magic words that spread kindness",
        "moral": "Always say \"Please\" and \"Thank You.\" Good manners show kindness and respect, and make everyone feel happy.",
        "p1": "There was a little girl named Emma who was cheerful and loved playing with her friends. She was smart and kind, but sometimes she forgot to use the magic words \"Please\" and \"Thank You.\" Whenever she wanted something, she would simply say, \"Give me the toy,\" or \"I want some juice.\" Although she did not mean to be rude, her words sometimes made others feel unhappy.",
        "p2": "One day, Emma's teacher told the class that \"Please\" and \"Thank You\" are magical words. They do not create real magic, but they make people feel happy, respected, and appreciated. The teacher explained that good manners help us make friends and show kindness to others.",
        "p3": "After school, Emma decided to try using the magic words. She smiled and said, \"Mom, may I please have some water?\" Her mother smiled warmly and gave her a glass of water. Emma happily replied, \"Thank you, Mom!\" Her mother gave her a big hug and said, \"You are very welcome.\"",
        "p4": "The next day, Emma asked her friend, \"May I please play with your ball?\" Her friend smiled and said, \"Of course!\" After playing together, Emma returned the ball and said, \"Thank you for sharing.\" Her friend felt happy because Emma was polite and respectful.",
        "p5": "Soon, Emma noticed that people smiled more when she used kind words. Her teachers, friends, and family were always happy to help her because she spoke with respect and gratitude. From that day on, Emma remembered to say \"Please\" whenever she asked for something and \"Thank You\" whenever someone helped her. She learned that these simple words can make every day brighter and every friendship stronger."
      },
      "clever_merchants": {
        "title": "The Clever Merchants",
        "subtitle": "Courage and wit win the day",
        "moral": "Even in a difficult situation, do not panic. Face problems bravely and make wise, clever decisions.",
        "p1": "In a village lived some merchants who often travelled to different places to sell their goods. One day, while they were going to sell their goods, it became very late. They had to pass through a dark forest at night. Some robbers stopped them and stole all their goods.",
        "p2": "The merchants were brave and clever. They thought of a smart plan. They told the robbers that they were excellent performers and would entertain them with a wonderful play. The robbers agreed and sat down to watch.",
        "p3": "The merchants began their play. First, they dressed as shepherds and sang, \"Here come the merchant performers, wearing a shepherd's costume.\" They acted as shepherds, then as carpenters, cobblers, and blacksmiths, and kept the robbers amused.",
        "p4": "The robbers became so happy that they began to dance and sing with the merchants. Then the merchants started a play about thieves and police. Some merchants acted as thieves, and some acted as police. They showed how the police come and catch the robbers. The performers sang, \"Here come the merchant performers, wearing a thief's costume. Run quickly, brother, run quickly — go and tell the police!\"",
        "p5": "Some merchants quietly went to the town and informed the real police about the robbers. The real police came back with them to the place where the play was going on. The merchants then sang, \"Here come the merchant performers, wearing a police costume.\" The merchants dressed as police arrived, and the robbers thought this was still part of the play, so they kept dancing. Just then, the real police arrived and caught the robbers. The robbers still believed it was only a play! The police took the robbers to jail, and the merchants got their goods back. This story teaches us that even in a bad situation, we should not be afraid. We should face problems with courage and make clever, correct decisions."
      },
      "magical_balloon": {
        "title": "The Magical Balloon Adventure",
        "subtitle": "A rainbow ride above the clouds",
        "moral": "Imagination can turn an ordinary day into an amazing adventure.",
        "p1": "One sunny morning, a curious little girl named Mia was playing in the park when she noticed a beautiful rainbow-colored balloon floating near a tree. It was unlike any balloon she had ever seen. Tiny sparkles danced around it, and it gently swayed in the breeze as if it were waiting for someone.",
        "p2": "As soon as Mia held the balloon's string, something amazing happened. The balloon began to glow, and slowly it lifted her into the air. Mia wasn't scared at all. She felt as if she were floating on a soft cloud. Higher and higher they went, flying above green fields, winding rivers, and colorful gardens.",
        "p3": "Their first stop was Candy Cloud Island, a magical place high in the sky. The clouds looked like cotton candy, chocolate rivers flowed through the land, and giant lollipops grew like trees. Mia played with friendly candy creatures, jumped on marshmallow hills, and enjoyed a delicious rainbow cupcake.",
        "p4": "Next, the balloon carried her to the Rainbow Waterfall. Instead of water, colorful streams of light flowed down sparkling cliffs. Mia slid down a rainbow, bounced on fluffy clouds, and chased glowing butterflies that painted colors in the sky wherever they flew.",
        "p5": "Then they visited the Starry Sky Playground, where children from magical lands played among twinkling stars. Mia rode a flying swing, hopped across moon-shaped stepping stones, and laughed as tiny star birds sang cheerful songs. As the sun began to set, the magical balloon gently carried Mia back to the park. Before floating away, it twinkled brightly and drew a shining heart in the sky. Mia waved goodbye with a smile, knowing she would never forget her wonderful adventure among the clouds, rainbows, and stars."
      },
      "lost_baby_dinosaur": {
        "title": "The Lost Baby Dinosaur",
        "subtitle": "A journey home filled with new friends",
        "moral": "Every adventure becomes more exciting when you meet new friends along the way.",
        "p1": "Deep inside a bright and colorful valley, a little baby dinosaur named Dino loved to explore. He was cheerful, playful, and always curious about everything around him. One morning, while chasing a group of colorful butterflies, Dino wandered farther and farther from home.",
        "p2": "After a while, Dino stopped and looked around. The butterflies had disappeared, and he could not see his family anywhere. The valley suddenly looked very different. Dino realized that he was lost. Feeling worried, he began searching for his way home. Along the way, he met a friendly parrot sitting on a tree branch. \"Have you seen my family?\" Dino asked. The parrot thought for a moment and pointed toward a sparkling river. \"I saw some dinosaurs near the river this morning,\" he said.",
        "p3": "Dino thanked the parrot and hurried toward the river. When he arrived, he found a group of turtles swimming happily, but his family was not there. One of the turtles suggested that he check the Flower Hills nearby. At the Flower Hills, Dino met a cheerful rabbit who was hopping through giant flowers. The rabbit had not seen Dino's family either, but he offered to help. Together they followed a trail of large dinosaur footprints leading through the valley.",
        "p4": "The footprints led them to a beautiful meadow filled with bright flowers and tall trees. Suddenly, Dino heard a familiar voice calling his name. \"Dino!\" It was his family! They had been searching everywhere for him. Dino ran as fast as he could and gave his family a big hug. Everyone was happy to be together again.",
        "p5": "That evening, the dinosaurs celebrated with a picnic under the stars. Dino told everyone about the parrot, the turtles, and the rabbit who had helped him on his journey. As he looked up at the twinkling sky, he smiled, knowing he had made many new friends during his adventure."
      }
    }
  },
